Conclusion:
In general, Blink shows how digital payments are developing in Mauritius. As a telecom wallet, it runs on a mobile app with its own structure and security features. It also relies on its user base and trust. Banks, telecoms, and regulators all are making their contributions to this evolving industry. Yet risks such as fraud, a small population, and strong rivals mean that to stay competitive, Blink must focus on what it does best and handle these risks smartly. If it succeeds, more people will gain trust, helping Blink grow and reach even more people.  
